 "text": {
  "asOf": "2026-11-06",
  "fixed": [
   "Tideline asks whether NEAR Intents fees could ever cover the new NEAR being issued. This is research, not financial advice.",
   "A Bullish reading means the evidence passed a line set in advance, not that the price will rise."
  ],
  "live": [
   "As of 6 Nov, the verdict is held at Undecided because flow went private. The score is +3 of 7, but data lost to private flow may not move the verdict, so it stays Undecided until the treasury share falls back to 50% or less.",
   "Pointing Bullish: NEAR's share of fees is 33% over the last 30 days and revenue has risen over each of the last three months. In between: one integrator brings much of the fees but stays under the 80% line (SwapKit 75% of visible app fees). The DefiLlama figures come from a dataset nobody can re-run for free.",
   "Not measured yet: Pricing Power (0 usable fee changes, 3 needed). Not measured because flow went private: Solver Competition (treasury 64% of USD). On the public swaps left, as side figures that set no reading: spread 10.4 bps and top 3 solvers hold 65%.",
   "The Confidential Intents treasury, where funds move to a private chain and the swap settles out of public view, carried 64% of the USD counted over the last 7 frozen days and 19% over the last 30.",
   "Monthly volume would need to reach about 3.2x today's level under the 1.6% issuance plan, which passed its vote but is not in force yet, or 5.1x if issuance stays at 2.5%, with all revenue spent on buybacks."
  ]
 }
